{"type":"block","data":{"id":"adoctext1000000000000000000","parentId":"adoccard1000000000000000000","rootId":"bdoc00000000000000000000000","createdBy":"system","modifiedBy":"system","schema":1,"type":"text","title":"## How this works\n\n1. Set up a folder for the agent to work in — the app asks for one when the board is set up.\n2. Make a card and describe the task in it the way you would explain it to a person: what is needed, and how to tell it is done.\n3. Put an agent in the card’s «Who is on it» field and drag the card into the «Agent writes» column: the move is what starts the agent. If it has a question, the question appears on the card.\n4. When it finishes, the agent moves the card on itself, into the column whose name says what happened. What it made is in the folder.\n\nThis card can be deleted — it starts nothing.\n\nThe folder for this board is the documentation repository. The agent writes on a branch of its own per card: nothing changes on the main branch until you merge it, and the branch name is on the card.","fields":{},"createAt":1785888000000,"updateAt":1785888000000,"deleteAt":0}}
